  "content": "# Bounded LRU Cache in Python: A Complete Tutorial\n\nAn **LRU (Least Recently Used) cache** is a data structure that evicts the least recently used item when its capacity is exceeded. Python's `collections.OrderedDict` is ideal for this because it maintains insertion order and provides O(1) operations for moving items to the end.\n\n## Core Concept\n\nThe key insight is that `OrderedDict` preserves insertion order, and we can:\n1. Move an item to the end when it's accessed (making it \"most recently used\")\n2. Pop from the front when the cache is full (evicting the \"least recently used\")\n\n## Complete Implementation\n\n```python\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\nfrom typing import Any, Hashable, Optional\n\n\nclass LRUCache:\n    \"\"\"\n    A bounded LRU cache using OrderedDict for O(1) get and put operations.\n    \n    Capacity defines the maximum number of keys the cache can hold.\n    When capacity is reached, the least recently used key is evicted.\n    \n    Thread-safety: NOT thread-safe by default. Use threading.Lock if needed.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    def __init__(self, capacity: int):\n        \"\"\"\n        Initialize the LRU cache with a given capacity.\n        \n        Args:\n            capacity: Maximum number of items the cache can hold.\n                      Must be positive.\n        \n        Raises:\n            ValueError: If capacity is less than 1.\n        \"\"\"\n        if capacity < 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"Capacity must be at least 1\")\n        \n        self.capacity = capacity\n        self.cache = OrderedDict()  # key -> value, ordered by recency\n    \n    def get(self, key: Hashable) -> Optional[Any]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Retrieve the value associated with the given key.\n        \n        If the key exists in the cache:\n        - The item is moved to the end (marking it as most recently used)\n        - Its value is returned\n        \n        If the key does not exist:\n        - None is returned\n        - No eviction occurs\n        \n        Time complexity: O(1)\n        Space complexity: O(1)\n        \n        Args:\n            key: A hashable key to look up.\n        \n        Returns:\n            The value associated with the key, or None if not found.\n        \"\"\"\n        if key not in self.cache:",
